## Origin branch — commit source (Release PR & Hotfix PR)

**Release PR** and **Hotfix PR** cherry-pick merge commits from a remote integration branch. **This repository** uses **`testing`** as the primary integration branch; **`staging`** remains available when commits landed there instead.

### Mandatory confirmation — origin branch

After candidate tasks are confirmed (Release step 1 / Hotfix step 1) and **before** commit lookup, fix-version lookup (Release only), or any `git checkout` / cherry-pick, use **`AskQuestion`**:

| Option | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **`testing`** | `git fetch origin testing` — commits from `git log origin/testing --grep=<ticket>` — **default for this team** |
| **`staging`** | `git fetch origin staging` — commits from `git log origin/staging --grep=<ticket>` |
| **`other`** | User names another remote branch (e.g. `develop`) in chat |

- Show the branch you plan to use and **why** (user request, team convention, or ticket environment).
- **Default to `testing`** in the question prompt for this repository — still require explicit confirmation; do not skip **`AskQuestion`** even if the user said "start release" or a prior turn used `testing`.
- If the user already named the origin branch in the **same message** (e.g. "use staging"), still confirm with **`AskQuestion`** (pre-select that option in the prompt text).
- Record the confirmed name as **`<origin-branch>`** (no `origin/` prefix) for the rest of the flow.

**Exception — y-git-workflow new path:** when invoked from **[`y-git-workflow.mdc`](y-git-workflow.mdc)** N11 on the **new** workflow, **do not** use this testing/staging table as the first origin question. N11 already ran **Cherry-pick source** (default **task branch `VAP-xxxx`**). Use that confirmed **`<origin-branch>`**. Commit lookup is `git log <origin-ref> --grep=<ticket>` where `<origin-ref>` is `origin/<origin-branch>` if it exists, else the local branch of the same name. Fetch `origin production` always; fetch `origin <origin-branch>` when that remote branch exists. **Legacy** workflow and standalone `/y-git-create-pr` still use the testing/staging table above (default **`testing`**).

### How `<origin-branch>` is used

| PR type | Usage |
|---------|--------|
| **Release PR** | `git fetch origin production` (and `origin/<origin-branch>` when it exists) → create `release-<version>` from **`origin/production`** when `<origin-branch>` is a **task branch** (`VAP-xxxx`); otherwise the existing flow (create from `origin/<origin-branch>` then `reset --hard origin/production` when scoping) → cherry-pick commits from **`<origin-ref>`** |
| **Hotfix PR** | `git fetch origin production` (and `origin/<origin-branch>` when it exists) → cherry-pick from **`<origin-ref>`** onto `prod-*` (still branch **from** `origin/production`) |

**`<origin-ref>`:** `origin/<origin-branch>` if that remote branch exists; otherwise the local branch of the same name (typical for new-path **`VAP-xxxx`**).

Cherry-pick **order** follows history on **`<origin-ref>`** (oldest first among selected commits).

**Task PR** merge destination stays **`testing`** by default ([Task PR — target branch](#task-pr--target-branch)); Task PR scope comparison also uses **`origin/testing`** unless the user confirms **`other`** for an unusual comparison base.

