## Release PR — PR workflow

Same structure as [Task PR — PR workflow](#task-pr--pr-workflow). Follow **`.github/pull_request_template.md`** for section headings.

### PR draft must be visible before draft approval (hard gate)

**Never** use **`AskQuestion`** for checklist confirmation, PR title/body approval (Release step 8, Hotfix step 7, Task step 11, or final approval), or calendar meeting draft approval until the **same assistant message** already contains:

1. A fenced code block with the **full PR title** (single line) — or calendar **title** in a `text` code block per **y-agt-gc-meet-helper**.
2. A fenced code block with the **full PR body** (all template sections, with proposed checklist and deployment defaults) — or calendar **description** under **`### Description (copy from here)`**.

**Checklist questions are not an exception** — show the full PR draft (with proposed checklist defaults) **before** Required/Optional checklist **`AskQuestion`** boxes.

If the user says you skipped the draft, **stop**, paste both blocks, then ask for approval again. Do **not** ask reviewers, git commands, or **`gh pr create`** in a turn that omits these two blocks when draft approval is on the agenda.

1. **Output format (two code blocks) before confirmations:**
   - **First** — **PR title alone** in its own fenced code block (single line).
   - **Second** — **full PR body** (all template sections) in a **draft** fenced code block — use **proposed defaults** for checklists and deployment notes; the user confirms or edits these via question boxes before the final body is locked in.

2. **Show draft before confirmations:** present the full suggested PR draft (title + body with proposed checklist and deployment defaults) **before** any confirmation question boxes — especially **before** step 8 “PR title + body” **`AskQuestion`**.

3. **Mandatory confirmation before PR creation:** only **after** both code blocks are in the message, confirm **PR title** and **PR body** (including finalized checklists and deployment notes) via **`AskQuestion`** (approve / edit). Revise and re-confirm if the user requests edits.

4. **Mandatory reviewers + self-assignment:**
   - Collect reviewers via **`AskQuestion`** (multi-select, **at least 5** suggested GitHub usernames + **`other`** if needed).
   - Require **at least one** reviewer before creating the PR.
   - Always self-assign (`@me`) when opening/updating the PR.

---

## Checklists — mandatory user input via question boxes

Applies to **Task PR, Hotfix PR, and Release PR**. Do **not** silently finalize checklist checkboxes. Use **`AskQuestion`** for **each checklist section** separately, with **pre-filled defaults** so the user can confirm quickly or change individual items.

**Hard gate:** the user must already see the **full PR draft** (title + body code blocks with these proposed defaults) in the **same or a prior message** before any checklist **`AskQuestion`**. See [PR draft must be visible before draft approval](#pr-draft-must-be-visible-before-draft-approval-hard-gate).

### ✅ Required Checklist — one `AskQuestion`

Present all five items with suggested checked/unchecked state. Use **multi-select** (or equivalent) so the user can toggle any item. Defaults:

| Item | Default |
|------|---------|
| Manual testing completed in local environment | **checked** (`- [x]`) |
| Tested in marketplace environment (if merging to production) | **unchecked** (`- [ ]`) |
| Code follows project style guidelines (Ruff linting passes) | **checked** |
| Self-review completed | **checked** |
| Docker builds successfully verified | **checked** |

After the user answers, render the **Required Checklist** section using their choices (`- [x]` / `- [ ]`).

### 📋 Optional Checklist (if applicable) — one `AskQuestion`

Present all four items with suggested defaults **informed by the release diff** (see [Release PR — Deployment Notes](#release-pr--deployment-notes)). Use **multi-select** (or equivalent). Defaults:

| Item | Default when diff suggests… |
|------|----------------------------|
| Tests added/updated and passing | **checked** if test files changed; else **unchecked** |
| Database migrations created | **checked** if migration files changed; else **unchecked** |
| Documentation updated | **checked** if `docs/` or README changed; else **unchecked** |
| Environment variables updated | **checked** if `.env.example`, env helpers, or config env keys changed; else **unchecked** |

After the user answers, render the **Optional Checklist** section using their choices.

If the user changes any default in either question box, use their answer — do not revert to silent defaults.

