## Release PR — PR title (CI)

Must pass **`.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml`** (“Validate PR Title”):

```text
<type>(VAP-0000): <release task 1> <release task 2> … [+ <dep task 1> <dep task 2> …]
```

- Use the literal placeholder scope **`VAP-0000`** in parentheses for multi-ticket release PRs.
- List every **release-candidate** Jira ticket (the user-supplied list) after the colon, **space-separated**, **ascending ticket number** unless the user asks for another order.
- **When the release branch also carries dependency cherry-picks** (the tickets recorded under **⚠️ Included via dependency (cherry-pick)** in the Description), append them after a single **` + `** separator (one space, plus sign, one space). Keep dependency tickets in **ascending ticket number** order among themselves. Use **exactly one** `+` separator — release tickets first, dependency tickets last.
- **Omit the `+ <dep …>` segment** when no dependency commits were added.
- Both sides of the `+` must contain at least one ticket. If there are no release-candidate tickets but only dependency cherry-picks, raise it with the user — that situation is unusual and likely a scoping mistake (do not just promote the deps).
- Valid types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.
- Examples:
  - Release tickets only: `feat(VAP-0000): VAP-1267 VAP-1345`
  - Release tickets **plus dependency cherry-picks**: `feat(VAP-0000): VAP-1267 VAP-1345 VAP-2998 + VAP-2417 VAP-2668`
- Do **not** use `VAP-1345: ...` without the `type(...)` wrapper.
- Do **not** mix release and dependency tickets on the same side of `+`. Do **not** use `,`, `&`, `/`, or any separator other than a single space within a side, and a single ` + ` between sides.

