## Release PR — Description template (per-task summaries required)

Under **📝 Description**, include a short intro line for the release, then **one summary block per Jira task** in the PR title (same order as the title).

Use the **same per-task block format** everywhere task text appears in the PR body (release scope and dependency section).

**Title ↔ body alignment:** the **release-candidate** tickets (left of `+` in the title) appear directly under **📝 Description** in title order. The **dependency** tickets (right of `+` in the title) appear under **⚠️ Included via dependency (cherry-pick)** in the same ascending order they have in the title. The set of tickets in the title and the set in the body must match exactly.

**Required format per task:**

```markdown
**VAP-2438 — Evidence citation quality (Vendoroo Resident prompts)**
Tightens how the assistant fills the Evidence field: per-turn scope, avoiding stale or repeated citations, emergency vs non-emergency alignment, quoting only relevant clauses, and preferring short verbatim spans.
```

**Rules:**

- **Line 1 (bold):** `**VAP-xxxx — <headline>**` — Jira key, em dash, short headline from the Jira summary (or a clear paraphrase). Do not invent product claims.
- **Line 2 (plain):** One concise paragraph (1–3 sentences) — what changed and why, outcome-focused.
- Repeat once per task key in the title, in title order.
- Pull headlines and summaries from Jira issue text, commits, and PR context; do not paste checklist boilerplate.

**Full Description example (two tasks):**

```markdown
Production release for QA-approved ResiRoo tickets already merged to testing.

**VAP-1267 — Automatically use weather context in ResiROO emergency assessment instead of asking the resident**
Adds automatic outdoor weather lookup from property location and current time for emergency-rule evaluation, with a 3°F comparison buffer and fallback to asking the resident when lookup fails or the rule needs indoor temperature.

**VAP-1345 — Inform resident that we cannot contact a 3rd person**
When a resident asks ResiRoo to contact a third party, the assistant declines warmly for security reasons and keeps the conversation open with the contact on file instead of firing Stop Protocol.
```

---

### ⚠️ Included via dependency (cherry-pick) (under Description)

When cherry-pick onto `origin/production` requires **extra integration-branch commits** that are **not** in the user’s release candidate list, document them in a **subsection of 📝 Description** — **not** as a top-level `##` heading and **not** as a one-line list.

The same dependency tickets **must** also appear in the **PR title** after the ` + ` separator (see [Release PR — PR title (CI)](#release-pr--pr-title-ci) above). The two sides — title and body — must list the same dependency tickets in the same ascending order.

**Subsection heading (use exactly, inside Description):**

```markdown
### ⚠️ Included via dependency (cherry-pick)
```

**Intro line (one short paragraph):** State that these tickets were already on the integration branch (**`<origin-branch>`**), were **not** named as release candidates, but were cherry-picked because a release ticket depends on them (name which release ticket(s), e.g. “required for VAP-1267”).

**Do not use** a compact line such as: `Technical dependencies (already on testing, required for VAP-1267): VAP-2417, VAP-2668.`

**Per dependency task:** Use the **same block format** as release tasks (`**VAP-xxxx — headline**` + summary paragraph). After the summary, add one optional third line when helpful: `Required for: VAP-xxxx` (or several keys, space-separated).

**Ordering:** List dependency tasks in **ascending Jira key** order unless the user asks otherwise.

**Omit this section** when no dependency commits were added to the release branch.

**Example:**

```markdown
## 📝 Description

Production release for QA-approved ResiRoo tickets already merged to testing.

**VAP-1267 — …**
…

### ⚠️ Included via dependency (cherry-pick)

These tickets were already merged to the integration branch and are included so release commits apply cleanly on production. They were not part of the release candidate list.

**VAP-2417 — P1: Unify RabbitMQ and API Resiroo experience**
Centralizes Resiroo chat preparation through the API path (including `resiroo_preparation` and emergency-assessment wiring) so RabbitMQ and HTTP entry points share the same behavior.
Required for: VAP-1267

**VAP-2668 — Improve Resiroo fallback behavior when image analysis fails to avoid resend loops and preserve a smooth resident experience**
Hardens image-analysis failure handling in the shared preparation flow so residents are not stuck in resend loops when analysis fails.
Required for: VAP-1267
```

---

**Other Description fields:**

- **🔗 Related Jira Tickets** — link **every** ticket in the PR title **and** every dependency ticket from **⚠️ Included via dependency (cherry-pick)**: `https://vendoroo-dev.atlassian.net/browse/VAP-1234`
- **🚀 Deployment Notes** — follow [Release PR — Deployment Notes](#release-pr--deployment-notes) above; never default to `None` without reviewing the release diff
- **📸 Screenshots/Examples** — default exactly **`N/A`** unless UI/visual examples apply

