## What not to do (all PR paths)

- Do **not** finalize checklist checkboxes without **`AskQuestion`** for both Required and Optional sections.
- Do **not** set Deployment Notes to `None` without reviewing the PR diff for env/config/migration/non-automated post-deploy needs.
- Do **not** ask confirmation questions before showing the full suggested PR description/body (title block + body block first in the **same** message — see [PR draft must be visible before draft approval](#pr-draft-must-be-visible-before-draft-approval-hard-gate)). This includes **checklist** `AskQuestion` boxes — show the draft with proposed checklist defaults first.
- Do **not** run an **`AskQuestion`** whose only purpose is “approve PR title + body” if that message does not already include the title code block and the full body code block.
- Do **not** run shell commands without first explaining intent and getting confirmation via **`AskQuestion`** when the batch changes remotes or creates the PR.
- Do **not** run **`gh pr create`** before **final approval** — push may happen earlier, but PR creation on the remote **must wait** for the user's explicit final yes.
- Do **not** leave the PR without reviewers or without self-assignment (`@me`).
- Do **not** leave **Hotfix** or **Release** PR handoff with stashes **you created in this run** still on **`git stash list`** — pop them all per [Stash restore (mandatory)](#stash-restore-mandatory).
- Do **not** list commit hashes or internal git mechanics in the PR body unless a reviewer needs them.

### What not to do — Task PR only

See also [Task PR — what not to do](#task-pr--what-not-to-do).

- Do **not** start commit lookup or diff review before **`git fetch origin testing`**.
- Do **not** open a **Task PR** with `--base production` unless the user explicitly confirmed **`other`**.
- Do **not** silently assume uncommitted or staged local files are in the PR.
- Do **not** add **🧪 Local Tests Report** without user confirmation. When included, paste **report content** into the PR — not a local file path reviewers cannot open.
- Do **not** auto-send Slack or auto-transition Jira at the end of a Task PR — follow steps 10–11 and **y-slack-pr-ready-for-review.mdc**.
- Do **not** include **`:calendar: PR review meeting is already on your calendar`** in Slack until step 10 confirms the meeting exists.

### What not to do — Hotfix PR only

See also [Hotfix PR — what not to do](#hotfix-pr--what-not-to-do).

- Do **not** use `release-<version>` or Task PR branch patterns (`feature/`, `bugfix/`, etc.) for Hotfix PRs.
- Do **not** create the hotfix branch from `origin/testing` or `origin/staging`.
- Do **not** use Confluence release version lookup for Hotfix PRs.
- Do **not** use Hotfix PR for scheduled weekly releases.

### What not to do — Release PR only

- Do **not** commit or push unless the user clearly asks for git operations beyond this release flow.
- Do **not** assume any **`<origin-branch>`** as the commit source without [Origin branch confirmation](#origin-branch--commit-source-release-pr--hotfix-pr).
- Do **not** start branch work, commit lookup, or diff review before **`git fetch origin <origin-branch> production`** (with user-confirmed **`<origin-branch>`**).
- Do **not** create the release branch from `origin/production` — it must come from **`origin/<origin-branch>`** (after fetch).
- Do **not** open a **Release PR** with `--base staging` or `--base testing` — merge destination is **`production`**.
- Do **not** merge the whole integration branch → `production` directly — always use **`release-<version>`**.
- Do **not** use `prod-*` branch naming for Release PRs — use `release-<version>`.
- Do **not** skip Confluence version lookup or user confirmation for version / branch / target.
- Do **not** skip explicit user input for release candidate tasks.
- Do **not** document dependency tickets as a one-line comma-separated list — use **⚠️ Included via dependency (cherry-pick)** with full per-task blocks.
- Do **not** mix release-candidate and dependency Jira keys on the same side of the `+` separator in the PR title, and do **not** use any separator other than a single space within a side or a single ` + ` between sides.
- Do **not** omit the `+ <dep …>` segment from the PR title when the body’s **⚠️ Included via dependency (cherry-pick)** section is non-empty — title and body must agree.
- Do **not** use Hotfix PR (`prod-*`) for scheduled releases — use `release-<version>` instead.

### Deployment Notes (Task, Hotfix, and Release)

- Do **not** use diagrams, flowcharts, or tables in **🚀 Deployment Notes** — keep it simple.
- Do **not** abbreviate env var names in Deployment Notes (no `VAR_*` wildcard patterns).

