## Pitfalls

### Task PR

- **Dirty working tree:** staged or uncommitted files are easy to mistake for PR scope — always show `git log origin/testing..HEAD` and warn.
- **Prompt/KB-only changes:** use **`None`** in Deployment Notes unless the diff also adds env vars, migrations, or a non-automated manual step — do not mention routine deploy restarts.
- **Stale testing:** always fetch before commit lookup; do not use local `testing` SHAs without fetch.
- **E2E report in PR body:** confirm inclusion with the user; read the source file and **paste report content** into the collapsed section — never only a `cursor_workspace/...` path.
- **Slack after PR:** offer Calendar step (step 10) **before** Slack; never send the calendar line until the user confirms the meeting exists.
- **Manual Google Calendar:** when the user creates the meeting themselves, **wait** — do not chain Slack in the same turn without their **meeting is ready** confirmation.

### Hotfix PR

- **Same files across tickets:** wrong cherry-pick order increases conflicts; always mirror **`<origin-branch>`** order among the chosen commits.
- **Uncommitted work:** stash before switching branches; **always pop every stash you created in this hotfix run** before handoff ([Stash restore (mandatory)](#stash-restore-mandatory)).
- **Push / SSH failures:** fix remotes and retry; the local `prod-…` branch remains valid.
- **Hidden dependencies:** cherry-pick conflicts often mean missing commits on **`<origin-branch>`**; add them in **`<origin-branch>`** order and document per **⚠️ Included via dependency (cherry-pick)**.

### Release PR

- **Same files across tickets:** wrong cherry-pick order increases conflicts; always mirror **`<origin-branch>`** order among the chosen commits.
- **Uncommitted work:** user may be on a feature branch with a dirty tree — stash before switching branches; **always pop every stash you created in this release run** before handoff ([Stash restore (mandatory)](#stash-restore-mandatory)).
- **Empty squash merges:** some merge commits may be no-ops on cherry-pick; still verify final diff scope vs `origin/production`.
- **Stale integration branch:** always fetch `origin/<origin-branch>` before commit lookup; do not use local branch SHAs without fetch.
- **Wrong origin branch:** commits on `staging` vs `testing` differ — confirm origin branch before cherry-pick; do not mix SHAs from different branches.
- **Stale Confluence doc:** if the pending version is unclear, use **`other`** and let the user supply the version.
- **Hidden dependencies:** cherry-pick conflicts often mean missing commits on **`<origin-branch>`**; add them in **`<origin-branch>`** order, then document each dependency ticket in **⚠️ Included via dependency (cherry-pick)** before final PR approval.

Apply this rule whenever the user asks to **create a PR**, **open a PR**, **create a hotfix PR**, or **create a release PR** for **this** repository — start with **Choose PR type** (`AskQuestion`) unless they already specified **Task PR**, **Hotfix PR**, or **Release PR** explicitly in the same message.
